\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Sweet place: sweet place alone!
\par The court of God most high,
\par The heaven of heavens, the throne
\par Of spotless majesty!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par O happy place! When shall I be
\par My God, with Thee, to see Thy face?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. There dwells my Lord, my King,
\par Judged here unfit to live;
\par There angels to Him sing,
\par And lowly homage give.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par O happy place! When shall I be
\par My God, with Thee, to see Thy face?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. The patriarchs of old
\par There from their travels cease;
\par The prophets there behold
\par Their longed- for- Prince of Peace.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par O happy place! When shall I be
\par My God, with Thee, to see Thy face?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. The Lamb's apostles there,
\par I might with joy behold;
\par The harpers I might hear
\par Harping on harps of gold.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par O happy place! When shall I be
\par My God, with Thee, to see Thy face?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. The faithful martyrs, they
\par Within those courts are found;
\par All clothed in pure array,
\par Their scars with glory crowned.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par O happy place! When shall I be
\par My God, with Thee, to see Thy face?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Jerusalem on high
\par My song and city is,
\par My home whene'er I die,
\par The centre of my bliss.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par O happy place! When shall I be
\par My God, with Thee, to see Thy face?
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

